  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinS&E 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A research team wants to change how often patients come in for blood
    tests during a trial. Before making the change, this must be reviewed to ensure
    patient participants are still protected.


    <b>Which group must review and
    approve this change before it can be implemented?</b>'
  explanation: The IRB must review and approve any changes that could affect patient
    participant safety or rights, such as new tests, schedule changes, or updated
    consent forms. This review helps ensure the study remains ethical, transparent,
    and safe for all patient participants as it moves forward.
  correctAnswer: Institutional Review Board (IRB)
  incorrectAnswer1: Environmental Health & Safety (EHS)
  incorrectAnswer2: Study sponsor
  incorrectAnswer3: Scientific Review Committee (SRC)
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Clinical
